# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
/target/

# Generated by Tauri
# will have schema files for capabilities auto-completion
/gen/schemas

# [Why gen/android IS committed] It stopped being a pure generated tree the moment the app
# needed native Android code. It now carries three hand-owned files that the app cannot run
# without:
#
#   app/src/main/java/com/arounder/hifishifter/NativeBridgePlugin.kt
#       system file picker (SAF), safe-area insets, system bar appearance
#   app/src/main/java/com/arounder/hifishifter/MainActivity.kt
#       edge-to-edge, back-gesture routing
#   app/src/main/res/values/ic_launcher_background.xml
#       adaptive-icon background colour
#
# Tauri only supports app-level Kotlin inside this directory, and `tauri android init`
# refuses to overwrite an existing project -- so a gitignored tree would mean every fresh
# clone silently lacks the bridge: the Rust side logs one error and the picker plus the
# safe-area handling are gone, with no build failure to point at it. `tauri android dev`
# does not run scripts/build/android.ps1 either, so an overlay applied only by that script
# would leave dev builds broken while release builds worked.
#
# Everything in there that IS still generated stays ignored -- see the generated project's
# own .gitignore files (gen/android/.gitignore, gen/android/app/.gitignore): build outputs,
# .gradle, tauri.settings.gradle, tauri.build.gradle.kts, tauri.properties,
# app/src/main/**/generated, jniLibs/**/*.so and assets/tauri.conf.json.
#
# [minSdk lives in two places now] tauri.conf.json's bundle.android.minSdkVersion is only
# read by `tauri android init`; with the project committed, app/build.gradle.kts is the
# truth. Keep the two in sync (they are both 26 today, for the AAudio reason documented
# there).
/gen/apple

# Staged ONNX Runtime dylibs for macOS bundling (generated by build.rs)
/resources/macos/

# Third-party build artifacts (CMake/MSBuild)
/third_party/world/build_world_dll/_build/
/third_party/world/build_world_dll/_build_*/

# Third-party source code (static linking - embedded as source code in the repo)
# Note: rubberband-static/ has been removed (replaced by signalsmith-stretch)
# Generated at build time by build.rs (CoreML-compatible variant)
backend/src-tauri/resources/models/nsf_hifigan/pc_nsf_hifigan_coreml.onnx
